          "answer": "w3a",
          "solutionReview": {
            "headline": "The vertex of a parabola is the point where it turns: here its lowest point.",
            "reasoning": [
              "The graph is a U-shaped parabola that opens upward, so its vertex is its lowest point.",
              "It crosses the x-axis at (0, 0) and (4, 0). It is lowest halfway between them, at x-coordinate (0 + 4) ÷ 2 = 2, where it is 4 units below the x-axis.",
              "So the vertex is (2, -4)."
            ],
            "answerSummary": "The vertex is (2, -4)."
          }
        },
