            },
            {
              "id": "decay",
              "label": "Exponential decay"
            }
          ],
          "solutionReview": {
            "headline": "Read two points one step apart: if the height is multiplied by more than 1 the graph rises (growth); by less than 1, it falls (decay).",
            "reasoning": [
              "Figure 1 goes through (0, 1) and (1, 2): its height doubles with each step to the right, so it rises. Exponential growth.",
              "Figure 2 goes through (0, 8) and (1, 4): its height halves with each step to the right, so it falls. Exponential decay.",
              "Figure 3 goes through (0, 1) and (1, 3): its height triples with each step to the right, so it rises. Exponential growth.",
              "Figure 4 goes through (0, 12) and (1, 3): its height is divided by 4 with each step to the right, so it falls. Exponential decay.",
              "Figure 5 goes through (0, 3) and (1, 6): its height doubles with each step to the right, so it rises. Exponential growth.",
              "Figure 6 goes through (0, 15) and (1, 7.5): its height halves with each step to the right, so it falls. Exponential decay."
            ],
            "answerSummary": "Exponential growth: figures 1, 3 and 5. Exponential decay: figures 2, 4 and 6."
          }
        }
      ]
