          "correctIndependentId": "boxes",
          "correctDependentId": "weight",
          "answerModel": {
            "equation": "f(x)=4x",
            "domain": "{0, 1, 2, ..., 30}",
            "range": "{0, 4, 8, ..., 120}",
            "continuity": "discrete"
          },
          "solutionReview": {
            "headline": "Boxes come only in whole numbers, so the student’s claim is not correct: the domain and the range are lists of separate values.",
            "reasoning": [
              "Discrete or continuous: x counts boxes, and the van cannot carry part of a box, so the relationship is discrete. The student’s claim, every real number from 0 to 30, would include 2.5 boxes, so it is not correct.",
              "Domain: from 0 boxes up to at most 30, in whole numbers, so the domain is {0, 1, 2, ..., 30}.",
              "Range: each box adds 4 pounds, so the weight is 4 times the number of boxes: 4 · 0 = 0, 4 · 1 = 4, 4 · 2 = 8, and so on up to 4 · 30 = 120, so the range is {0, 4, 8, ..., 120}."
            ],
            "answerSummary": "The claim is not correct: the relationship is discrete, with domain {0, 1, 2, ..., 30} and range {0, 4, 8, ..., 120}."
          }
        }
